-- Repro: stdlib sleep() rejects an int literal arg.
--
-- The stdlib template at src/ast/std_lib.rb:
--   "sleep" => { args: [:Int64], return: :Void,
--                zig: "rt.sleep(@intCast(@as(u64, @bitCast({0}))))" }
-- expands `sleep(1)` to `rt.sleep(@intCast(@as(u64, @bitCast(1))))`.
-- Zig rejects: "cannot @bitCast from 'comptime_int'".
--
-- The annotator knows the literal `1` would be coerced to Int64 at
-- the call boundary (the param is declared :Int64), but the template
-- substitution loses that context. Either the template needs to wrap
-- the arg in `@as(i64, ...)` itself, or the call-site emitter must
-- coerce literal numeric args to the declared param type before
-- substitution.
--
-- The bug bit _bc_runner.cht's lock_acquire spin-wait (Phase B/C):
--   sleep(1);
-- which never compiled. Worked around in commit 1bc679ec by binding
-- to a typed local first:
--   sleepArg: Int64 = 1_i64; sleep(sleepArg);

FN main() RETURNS Void ->
    sleep(1);
END
